    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0366" n="260" xml:id="pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.00B Communist International of Youth/16:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Shantz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-26T13:00:00+03:00">September 26,
                            1935—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 26—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>439. Sixth Congress of Communist International of Youth opened in Moscow
                    September 25th. Following United States delegates were elected to Presidium:
                    Green, Lightfoot and Porter. Pieck, Dimitrov and Kuusinen were present at the
                    first session. Raymond Guillot [<hi rendition="#italic">Guyot</hi>] (French)
                    made opening speech.</p>
                <p>Embassy will follow sessions closely.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shantz</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
